{"step_index":324,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T19:44:01Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T21:44:01+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T21:44:01+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/Madziva/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/qualification-verification-system/src/main/java/com/devops/qvs/service/AiFraudDetectionService.java`\nTotal Lines: 308\nTotal Bytes: 17063\nShowing lines 1 to 200\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: package com.devops.qvs.service;\n2: \n3: import com.devops.qvs.dto.AiAnalysisResultDto;\n4: import com.devops.qvs.dto.AiChatRequest;\n5: import com.devops.qvs.dto.AiChatResponse;\n6: import com.devops.qvs.model.Qualification;\n7: import com.devops.qvs.model.QualificationStatus;\n8: import com.devops.qvs.repository.QualificationRepository;\n9: import lombok.RequiredArgsConstructor;\n10: import lombok.extern.slf4j.Slf4j;\n11: import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;\n12: \n13: import java.time.LocalDate;\n14: import java.time.LocalDateTime;\n15: import java.util.ArrayList;\n16: import java.util.List;\n17: import java.util.Optional;\n18: \n19: @Service\n20: @RequiredArgsConstructor\n21: @Slf4j\n22: public class AiFraudDetectionService {\n23: \n24:     private final QualificationRepository qualificationRepository;\n25:     private final CryptoHashService cryptoHashService;\n26: \n27:     /**\n28:      * Executes multi-vector AI heuristic fraud and anomaly analysis on a certificate.\n29:      */\n30:     public AiAnalysisResultDto analyzeCertificate(String certificateNumber) {\n31:         log.info(\"Agentic AI Fraud Detection initiated for certificate: {}\", certificateNumber);\n32:         Optional<Qualification> qualOpt = qualificationRepository.findByCertificateNumber(certificateNumber.trim());\n33: \n34:         List<String> anomalyFlags = new ArrayList<>();\n35:         List<String> passedChecks = new ArrayList<>();\n36:         int score = 100;\n37:         String riskLevel = \"LOW\";\n38:         double confidence = 98.5;\n39: \n40:         if (qualOpt.isEmpty()) {\n41:             anomalyFlags.add(\"CRITICAL: Certificate number does not exist in any accredited institutional registry.\");\n42:             anomalyFlags.add(\"HIGH: Zero cryptographic signature match found in national qualification ledger.\");\n43:             return AiAnalysisResultDto.builder()\n44:                     .certificateNumber(certificateNumber)\n45:                     .authenticityScore(0)\n46:                     .riskLevel(\"CRITICAL\")\n47:                     .confidencePercentage(99.0)\n48:                     .anomalyFlags(anomalyFlags)\n49:                     .passedChecks(List.of())\n50:                     .recommendation(\"REJECT CREDENTIAL: High probability of forged or fraudulent certificate document.\")\n51:                     .agentExplanation(\"AI Agent Evaluation: The certificate number was not found in the verified database. No cryptographic hash exists to corroborate institutional issuance.\")\n52:                     .analyzedAt(LocalDateTime.now())\n53:                     .build();\n54:         }\n55: \n56:         Qualification qual = qualOpt.get();\n57: \n58:         // 1. Check Cryptographic Fingerprint Integrity\n59:         boolean fingerprintValid = cryptoHashService.verifyFingerprint(\n60:                 qual.getCertificateNumber(),\n61:                 qual.getStudentFullName(),\n62:                 qual.getStudentIdNumber(),\n63:                 qual.getAwardTitle(),\n64:                 qual.getInstitution().getInstitutionCode(),\n65:                 qual.getAwardDate(),\n66:                 qual.getDigitalFingerprint()\n67:         );\n68: \n69:         if (fingerprintValid) {\n70:             passedChecks.add(\"Cryptographic Integrity: Deterministic SHA-256 digital fingerprint verified (No payload tampering detected).\");\n71:         } else {\n72:             score -= 60;\n73:             anomalyFlags.add(\"CRITICAL: Cryptographic payload mismatch detected. Record fields have been tampered with or modified post-issuance.\");\n74:         }\n75: \n76:         // 2. Check Status\n77:         if (qual.getStatus() == QualificationStatus.ACTIVE) {\n78:             passedChecks.add(\"Institutional Standing: Credential is actively endorsed with zero disciplinary holds.\");\n79:         } else if (qual.getStatus() == QualificationStatus.REVOKED) {\n80:             score -= 75;\n81:             anomalyFlags.add(\"HIGH RISK: Credential has been officially REVOKED by awarding institution. Reason: \" + qual.getRevocationReason());\n82:         }\n83: \n84:         // 3. Check Award Date Consistency\n85:         if (qual.getAwardDate().isAfter(LocalDate.now())) {\n86:             score -= 40;\n87:             anomalyFlags.add(\"ANOMALY: Award date is in the future (\" + qual.getAwardDate() + \"). Impossible issuance timestamp.\");\n88:         } else if (qual.getAwardDate().isBefore(LocalDate.of(1950, 1, 1))) {\n89:             score -= 30;\n90:             anomalyFlags.add(\"WARNING: Historical award date predates digital system baselines (\" + qual.getAwardDate() + \").\");\n91:         } else {\n92:             passedChecks.add(\"Chronological Feasibility: Award date (\" + qual.getAwardDate() + \") conforms to standard academic calendar cycles.\");\n93:         }\n94: \n95:         // 4. Check Serial Number Formatting\n96:         if (qual.getCertificateNumber().matches(\"^QVS-\\\\d{4}-[A-Z]{3}-\\\\d{4}$\")) {\n97:             passedChecks.add(\"Pattern Recognition: Certificate serial number adheres to ISO-standard QVS cryptographic entropy scheme.\");\n98:         } else {\n99:             score -= 10;\n100:             anomalyFlags.add(\"NOTICE: Non-standard serial format detected; manual institutional validation recommended.\");\n101:         }\n102: \n103:         // 5. Check Institution Accreditation\n104:         if (qual.getInstitution() != null && qual.getInstitution().isActive()) {\n105:             passedChecks.add(\"Accreditation: Issued by verified accredited body '\" + qual.getInstitution().getName() + \"'.\");\n106:         } else {\n107:             score -= 50;\n108:             anomalyFlags.add(\"HIGH: Issuing body accreditation status is unverified or suspended.\");\n109:         }\n110: \n111:         // Determine Risk Level\n112:         score = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, score));\n113:         if (score >= 90) {\n114:             riskLevel = \"LOW\";\n115:         } else if (score >= 60) {\n116:             riskLevel = \"MEDIUM\";\n117:         } else if (score >= 30) {\n118:             riskLevel = \"HIGH\";\n119:         } else {\n120:             riskLevel = \"CRITICAL\";\n121:         }\n122: \n123:         String recommendation;\n124:         String explanation;\n125:         if (riskLevel.equals(\"LOW\")) {\n126:             recommendation = \"ACCEPT CREDENTIAL: Full confidence in academic authenticity and digital integrity.\";\n127:             explanation = \"AI Agent Evaluation: All security vectors passed with flying colors. No data tampering, valid cryptographic signature, and active institutional endorsement.\";\n128:         } else if (riskLevel.equals(\"MEDIUM\")) {\n129:             recommendation = \"CONDITIONAL REVIEW: Minor anomalies found. Verify original transcripts with registrar.\";\n130:             explanation = \"AI Agent Evaluation: Credential has minor formatting or historical metadata discrepancies.\";\n131:         } else {\n132:             recommendation = \"REJECT / ESCALATE: High risk of fraud, disciplinary revocation, or data tampering detected.\";\n133:             explanation = \"AI Agent Evaluation: Critical risk flags triggered. The certificate is either revoked or fails cryptographic proof verification.\";\n134:         }\n135: \n136:         return AiAnalysisResultDto.builder()\n137:                 .certificateNumber(qual.getCertificateNumber())\n138:                 .authenticityScore(score)\n139:                 .riskLevel(riskLevel)\n140:                 .confidencePercentage(confidence)\n141:                 .anomalyFlags(anomalyFlags)\n142:                 .passedChecks(passedChecks)\n143:                 .recommendation(recommendation)\n144:                 .agentExplanation(explanation)\n145:                 .analyzedAt(LocalDateTime.now())\n146:                 .build();\n147:     }\n148: \n149:     /**\n150:      * Conversational AI Assistant for natural language qualification queries.\n151:      */\n152:     /**\n153:      * Conversational AI Assistant for natural language qualification and role permission queries.\n154:      * Truly queries the institutional repository and blockchain state to eliminate hallucinations.\n155:      */\n156:     public AiChatResponse processUserQuery(AiChatRequest request) {\n157:         String rawMsg = request.getMessage() != null ? request.getMessage().trim() : \"\";\n158:         String msg = rawMsg.toLowerCase();\n159:         LocalDateTime now = LocalDateTime.now();\n160: \n161:         // 1. Role Access Levels and Permission Matrix\n162:         if (msg.contains(\"access\") || msg.contains(\"role\") || msg.contains(\"permission\")\n163:                 || msg.contains(\"difference\") || (msg.contains(\"admin\") && msg.contains(\"officer\"))) {\n164:             return AiChatResponse.builder()\n165:                     .reply(\"🛡️ **QVS Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) Matrix**:\\n\\n\"\n166:                             + \"1. **System Administrator (`ROLE_ADMIN`)**:\\n\"\n167:                             + \"   • **Full Master Authority**: Can register qualifications, inspect system audit trails, and access real-time JVM telemetry.\\n\"\n168:                             + \"   • **Exclusive Revocation Power**: Only Administrators have the authority to revoke credentials on the blockchain.\\n\\n\"\n169:                             + \"2. **Registrar Officer (`ROLE_INSTITUTION`)**:\\n\"\n170:                             + \"   • **Institutional Registrar**: Can issue new academic credentials for their university and manage the institutional registry.\\n\"\n171:                             + \"   • **Access Restrictions**: **Cannot revoke credentials** (disciplinary/admin authority required) and cannot view internal server telemetry or audit trails.\\n\\n\"\n172:                             + \"3. **Accredited Verifier (`ROLE_VERIFIER`)**:\\n\"\n173:                             + \"   • **Verification Specialist**: Can perform instant qualification verification, inspect blockchain blocks, and run AI anomaly scans.\\n\"\n174:                             + \"   • **Access Restrictions**: Cannot browse student registries, cannot issue credentials, and cannot revoke records.\")\n175:                     .intent(\"EXPLAIN_ACCESS_LEVELS\")\n176:                     .status(\"INFO\")\n177:                     .timestamp(now)\n178:                     .build();\n179:         }\n180: \n181:         // 2. How to Verify\n182:         if (msg.contains(\"how\") && (msg.contains(\"verify\") || msg.contains(\"check\") || msg.contains(\"lookup\"))) {\n183:             return AiChatResponse.builder()\n184:                     .reply(\"💡 **How to Verify a Certificate**:\\n\\n\"\n185:                             + \"1. **Sign In**: Log into the portal using your accredited Verifier, Officer, or Admin account.\\n\"\n186:                             + \"2. **Open Console**: Navigate to the **'Verify Credential'** tab on your dashboard.\\n\"\n187:                             + \"3. **Enter Identifier**: Enter the Certificate Serial Number (e.g. `QVS-2024-BSC-8891`) or SHA-256 hash.\\n\"\n188:                             + \"4. **Validate**: Click **'Verify Authenticity'** to inspect the real-time institutional match,